WEBVTT

NOTE F2: single participant; branches, two error flows (one returns, one can end the task), attempts, outcome frequency, threshold judgements. Late correction of the approval threshold (c18) and late detail on the first step (c19). Synthetic.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
<v Interviewer>Can you walk me through submitting an expense claim?</v>

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:18.000
<v Marcus Lee>Yeah. Mostly it's train tickets and hotels from client visits. I just want my money back before the credit card bill lands.</v>

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
<v Marcus Lee>First thing, I photograph all the receipts with my phone.</v>

4
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:35.000
<v Marcus Lee>Then I fill in the claim form in the expenses app and attach the photos.</v>

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
<v Interviewer>On a scale of one to five, where five is very hard, how hard is the form?</v>

6
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:49.000
<v Marcus Lee>I'd give it a three. The cost codes are confusing.</v>

7
00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:01.000
<v Marcus Lee>The annoying bit is the app rejects photos if they're even slightly blurry. That happens way too often.</v>

8
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Marcus Lee>So I have to retake the photo and attach it again. Usually takes three or four goes before it accepts it. Then I'm back on the form.</v>

9
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:24.000
<v Marcus Lee>Once it's submitted, if the claim is over fifty pounds, it goes to my manager to approve.</v>

10
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.000
<v Marcus Lee>If it's under fifty it goes straight to finance.</v>

11
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:37.000
<v Marcus Lee>My manager approves it in the app, normally within a day or two.</v>

12
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:49.000
<v Marcus Lee>Sometimes she just doesn't respond, maybe one claim in ten. Then I chase her by email.</v>

13
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:56.000
<v Marcus Lee>If she replies within the week, it carries on to finance as normal.</v>

14
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:08.000
<v Marcus Lee>If not, honestly, I've given up on the claim. That's happened twice this year, so it's not a big deal.</v>

15
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.000
<v Marcus Lee>Finance processes it and I get paid in the next payroll run.</v>

16
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.000
<v Interviewer>How long does the whole thing take you?</v>

17
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:28.000
<v Marcus Lee>My part, about twenty minutes a claim. I do one most months.</v>

18
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:38.000
<v Marcus Lee>Oh, I said fifty pounds for manager approval. Actually they raised it to a hundred in April, I keep forgetting.</v>

19
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:50.000
<v Marcus Lee>And going back to the photos: if it's a faded till receipt, I scan it on the office printer instead of using my phone.</v>
